Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: The Foghorn Bites the Pier
- Story & Context: Inside the suffocating projection booth of the Cine Marajó above the Santos shipping channel, Zé do Fita loaded an unreleased silent reel of phantom naval mutinies spliced together from discarded government scrap film. When the port military patrol hammered on the padlocked steel booth door with rifle butts, the room filled with the acrid stench of hot vinegar celluloid and scorching carbon lamps as Big Dênis pinned the deadbolt shut using a rusted tire iron. Instead of surrendering, Zé jammed his cracked ivory melodica directly into the booth's emergency intercom trumpet, unleashing an ear-splitting battle-cry over an eighty-eight BPM boom-bap break while Clara yelled into the talkback: "Burn the spool down to the sprocket, we don’t take your curfew ticket!" That four-minute standoff became the bootlegged master recording that birthed the genre across the docks before the patrol could breach the jamb.
